Now I laugh and tell them about a confusing Saturday.
It was at the end of January.
I wanted to go into the city center.
I walked over to the stop and took the bus.
But it was the wrong bus.
I rode for a long time.
Suddenly the bus stopped.
The driver looked at me and said: "We are at the final stop."
I stepped out onto the street.
It was a completely unknown neighborhood.
I looked at the map on my phone.
I was very far away from my apartment.
I walked around the area a bit.
There were many trees and small houses.
Finally, I found another stop.
I bought a new ticket for twenty-four kroner.
I waited fifteen minutes in the cold.
My brother Diego laughs loudly on the screen.
It was a silly mistake, but a good memory.
